
/** \page Introduction

!!! Introduction

!! Platinum and PPR

The Platinum C++ framework (www.platinum.ptv.de) is the origin of the Ptv
Portable Runtime. Platinum, or Pt for short, was started as an open source 
project (LGPL) in 2003 and the name is a pun on NIHCL, which was a popular
C++ toolkit in the past. 
In 2006 PTV AG started to use a slightly modified version of Pt as the 
foundation of its navi-platform. That was the birth of the Ptv Portable
Runtime or PPR, which is pronounced Pepper. This again is a pun on Mocca, a 
framework offered by one of its competitors.
For the most part the two versions are identical and the developers employed
by PTV AG are encouraged to commit code to Pt and develop it further.

*/

